Gas Insulated Switchgear consists of metal enclosed assemblies that encapsulate all live components within sealed chambers filled with sulfur hexafluoride (SF₆) gas. This configuration delivers high voltage isolation while achieving a significantly smaller footprint compared with conventional air insulated switchgear, making it ideal for high density urban substations, remote offshore wind farms, and long haul transmission corridors.
